# CODEOWNERS
#
# Maps paths in this repository to the GitHub users who should be requested
# as reviewers on a pull request that touches them. GitHub reads this file
# from `.github/CODEOWNERS`; the *last* matching pattern wins.
#
# Source of truth for ownership is the "Maintainers & Community" section of
# README.md, which names @Hollujay as the sole maintainer. Update this file
# whenever that section changes.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default: everything in the repository is owned by the maintainer, so every
# new pull request gets a reviewer automatically — including the ones from
# first-time contributors who do not know who to request.
*                       @Hollujay

# Critical paths are listed explicitly so a dedicated reviewer can be added
# per area later without disturbing the default above.

# Structural validator — the only executable surface in this repository.
/tools/validate/        @Hollujay

# Fixture JSON schema; changes here can invalidate every existing fixture.
/schemas/               @Hollujay

# CI, templates, and repository automation.
/.github/               @Hollujay
